package server

const mcpNotationPolicy = "Bridge 0.11.0 advertises standard-notations-v1. Five reusable collections are hipo, dfd-yourdon, dfd-gane-sarson, uml and bpmn; existing IBM flowchart discovery remains unchanged. GET /notation/collections returns public collection metadata; GET /notation/collections/{collectionId} adds schemaVersion:1, capability:standard-notations-v1, symbols and connectors. Exact /symbols and /connectors subpaths return their arrays with stable IDs, supported diagramKinds, applicable property descriptors and primary-source provenance. Use only the actual discovered symbol/property combinations; BPMN event contexts follow the supported source-backed matrix rather than every theoretical marker permutation. Optional diagram.notation={schemaVersion:1,collection,diagramKind}, node.notation and edge.notation retain semantic collection/symbol choices, compartments, custom ports, native node references, relationship end labels/multiplicities, applicable properties and bounded waypoints through ordinary graph CRUD. They do not add native diagram/node types or executable process semantics. Node notation retains existing nodeType and ordinary titles, backgrounds, owners and relationships. A node can have either notation or flowchartSymbol; clear the alternate field with null in the same versioned PATCH or existing bulk upsert when switching, or the complete edit returns 422 INVALID_NOTATION. Full/new records reject null, unsupported fields, collection/symbol combinations, properties, malformed or dangling references and bounds with structured 422 INVALID_NOTATION; invalid graph edits save nothing. A versioned entity PATCH or existing bulk upsert can use notation:null to remove the complete optional field; omission preserves it, and a supplied notation object replaces that field rather than recursively merging its properties. Read the graph and current entity versions before editing. Host moves through PATCH or bulk translate native group contents and attached ports, boundary events and executions once. Explicit child or attachment coordinates in the same bulk request take precedence independently of entry order; related-node links do not imply movement. Read the resulting graph and entity versions before subsequent edits. Native JSON, copy, templates, encryption, history, backups and collaboration preserve notation and remap native references. POST /diagrams/{diagramId}/notation/validate with no data or exactly {} is pure, permits Read only, and returns diagramId, baseVersion and semantic issues without writes; incomplete draft semantics are issues rather than guessed execution. Collection examples use POST /diagrams with an exact discovered supported template key, optional type:freeform, and no mode option. A supplied notation profile must exactly match the template; null, invalid or conflicting profiles reject before saving. New notation rooms pin CRDT document contract version 3, retained after clearing notation; older clients reject it before projection. Existing version-1/2 rooms reject adding notation with 409 COLLABORATION_NOTATION_REQUIRED; refresh all participants and create a new room. Owner authority and role checks remain unchanged. Process Simulator and Time Series & Signal Analysis retain specialized tools. Fixed HIPO ipo-chart layouts permit at most three compartments, or four when properties.detail is detail or node diagramKind is detail-ipo; BPMN choreography-task, sub-choreography and call-choreography permit three. Extra sections reject with 422 INVALID_NOTATION; valid custom section IDs and content are preserved. UML/BPMN graphical modeling is not a complete metamodel, XMI/BPMN XML interchange, execution engine or conformance certification."
